---
/**
 * About — who Poesis is, what it believes about organizations, where the method
 * comes from, and who answers for it. The full research argument lives in
 * Knowledge (/knowledge/thesis), unchanged.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { thesisPath } from '../data/knowledge.ts';
import { safLinks } from '../data/saf.ts';
import { externalLinkAttributes, externalLinks } from '../data/site.ts';

const title = 'About Poesis';
const description = 'Poesis is the company behind SAF, the open-source Systemic Agentic Framework. It treats an organization as a system that produces itself, and guides its agentic transformation.';

/** Names, roles, portraits and profile links are those already published on this site. */
const people: { name: string; role: string; photo: string; bio: string; profile?: string }[] = [
  {
    name: 'Clément Cazaud',
    role: 'Founder. Chief Executive, Product and Architecture Officer',
    photo: '/clement-cazaud.jpg',
    bio: 'Enterprise and solution architect and software engineer. He created the Generative System Model and the Poesis stack.',
    profile: 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/clement-cazaud',
  },
  {
    name: 'Brahim Ben Helal',
    role: 'Co-founder. Chief Growth Officer',
    photo: '/brahim-ben-helal.jpg',
    bio: 'A career in enterprise software and commercial strategy. He leads growth, ecosystem development and customer engagement.',
    // The profile address published before the redesign answered 404 on 2026-11-21: no link until Poesis confirms it.
    profile: undefined,
  },
  {
    name: 'Hamza Abidi',
    role: 'Co-founder. Chief Technology and Engineering Officer',
    photo: '/hamza-abidi.jpg',
    bio: 'He owns the technical foundations of Poesis and their engineering.',
    profile: 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/abidihamza',
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  pageType="About"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'About' }]}
  jsonLd={[{ '@type': 'AboutPage', name: title, url: 'https://poesis.cloud/about/', description }]}
>
  <section class="intro">
    <div class="container">
      <ol class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <li><a href="/">Poesis</a></li>
        <li aria-current="page">About</li>
      </ol>
      <h1>About Poesis.</h1>
      <p class="intro__lead">Poesis is the company behind SAF, the open-source Systemic Agentic Framework. It does one thing for its clients: it guides the agentic transformation of an organization, or of one of its parts.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--raised" aria-labelledby="vision-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="band-head">
        <h2 id="vision-title">An organization is a system that produces itself.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose-narrow">
        <p>Poiesis is the Greek word for bringing-forth. Maturana and Varela joined it to <em>auto</em>, self, to name what distinguishes living systems: they produce the components that produce them. An organization does the same. Its roles, rules and ways of working are what make the next version of it.</p>
        <p>Generative AI made production cheap. It did not supply what keeps self-production from becoming drift: an explicit definition of the organization that people own and that the work is held to. That is the gap Poesis works on. Poesis calls that definition the DNA of the organization, which is what its mark depicts.</p>
        <p>In practice this means a seed: a small, explicit model of roles, workflows and decision points, planted on a real scope, observed, and changed by what the work shows.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="origin-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="band-head">
        <h2 id="origin-title">Where the method comes from.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose-narrow">
        <p>The founders of Poesis spent their careers inside large IT estates: architecting them, governing them, and selling and scaling the platforms they run on. Every estate ran on definitions (architectures, obligations, processes, constraints) and kept them in documents that nothing could act on.</p>
        <p>The method draws on systemics: Beer’s Viable System Model, von Bertalanffy’s General System Theory, the cybernetics of Wiener and Ashby, and Maturana and Varela’s autopoiesis. Poesis does not claim to have invented that theory. Its contribution is to make it operable, first for agentic work with SAF.</p>
        <p>The research behind it is published as a chain of notes, each establishing one step of the argument.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={thesisPath}><Icon name="book-open" /> Read the thesis and its argument</a>
          <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/knowledge/">Browse the Knowledge base</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--raised" aria-labelledby="team-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="band-head">
        <h2 id="team-title">The people who answer for it.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="people">
        {people.map((person) => (
          <li class="person">
            <img src={person.photo} alt={`Portrait of ${person.name}`} width="72" height="72" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <h3>{person.name}</h3>
            <p class="person__role">{person.role}</p>
            <p>{person.bio}</p>
            {person.profile && <p><a href={person.profile} {...externalLinkAttributes}>{person.name.split(' ')[0]} on LinkedIn</a></p>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--tight" aria-labelledby="trust-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="band-head">
        <h2 id="trust-title">Where to check what we say.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="kb-links">
        <li><a href={externalLinks.github} {...externalLinkAttributes} data-track="developer_repo_click" data-track-id="about-trust">Poesis on GitHub</a><p>The code, its releases and its issues.</p></li>
        <li><a href={safLinks.docs} {...externalLinkAttributes} data-track="developer_docs_click" data-track-id="about-trust">SAF documentation</a><p>How the framework works and what it does not do yet.</p></li>
        <li><a href={externalLinks.linkedin} {...externalLinkAttributes}>Poesis on LinkedIn</a><p>The company page.</p></li>
        <li><a href="/legal/mentions-legales">Legal notice</a><p>Publisher and hosting information.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="closing-title">Talk to the people who build it.</h2>
      <p>Whether you are considering a transformation or working with SAF on your own, the conversation starts the same way.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/contact/" data-track="business_contact_intent" data-track-id="about-closing">Talk to Poesis</a>
        <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/transformation/">See the transformation service</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
